 recorded here. Starting picks draw from a levels 1-3 sublist (34 spells); each level from 2 to 15 grants two from the full list capped at the character''s level. MYSTIC MAGIC BONUSES: ''all other magic-related abilities work as per the mystic character class'' is not stored as numbers - whether the Mystic''s level-gated save vs magic and spell strength bonuses count as magic-related abilities is the G.M.''s reading, so they are prose in special_abilities. OCCULT LORE (+20%): no catalog skill carries that name and Nightbane''s skill list (printed 48) has none; offered as a choice of the book''s own Lore skills at +20%, the shape the Mystic O.C.C.''s ''one Lore skill of choice (+20%)'' takes. DRAGONESE: the +20% reads as belonging to the two languages of choice, not to Dragonese, which prints no figure. COMBAT: three attacks per melee at first level ''or two by magic''; the physical three is stored as attacks_base, the magic two is here. Levels four and eight add one attack each. BONUSES: the book prints +5 strike and +5 dodge in the air and +2 on the ground; the ground figure is stored and the air figure is prose. NUMBERS READ OFF A RENDER of printed 169, where the text layer garbles them: Horror Factor 8, bite 1D8, 8 secondary skills, weight 6.8 kg. MONEY AND EQUIPMENT: the entry prints neither."
