# Snake Bird

## Lore

Snake Birds look strikingly like the extinct feathered serpents of Earth: a rattlesnake-sized body with a pair of feathered wings and taloned legs near its midsection, body and wings brightly colored in solid blues, greens, reds and yellows or mottled, striped and spotted with those colors plus black and white. Unlike the true feathered serpents they are very powerful fliers.

They are sentient, speak in a squawking, amusing voice, and are believed to come from an alien dimension where most living creatures can speak. They are also accomplished spell casters who know a great deal of spell magic, much of it unknown on Earth. Lone hunters and predators, they hunt alone or, more rarely, in mated pairs; they need no food but keep strong predatory instincts. Some occultists believe they are a magical creation combining animal parts with a human mind.

Like humans, Snake Birds can be good, evil or indifferent. Most distrust humans and other bipeds, but some have become friends and "familiars" to magicians or Nightbane. Some evil Snake Birds have become "pets" of the Nightlords, using their magic to amuse the Ba''al by torturing humans and Dopplegangers.

## GM Notes

Average life span is 300 years. Habitat: any, preferring mountains; found in the Nightlands and occasionally on Earth and in other dimensions. Enemies: large predators, and the Nightlords and their minions.

As NPCs they average level 1D6+1, and a few reach near-legendary power at 12th level and up.
